{title: Simple Gifts}
{artist: Joseph Brackett}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{meta: public_domain Shaker song by Elder Joseph Brackett, written 1848.}
{meta: source Shaker manuscript, Alfred, Maine, 1848; printed in the 19th century in Shaker collections.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse}
'Tis the [G]gift to be simple, 'tis the [G]gift to be [D]free,
'Tis the [D]gift to come down where we [D]ought to [G]be,
And [G]when we find ourselves in the [G]place just [D]right,
'Twill be in the [D]valley of [D]love and de[G]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When true [C]simpli[G]city is [G]gained,
To [G]bow and to bend we [D]shan't be a[D]shamed,
To [G]turn, turn will [C]be our de[G]light,
Till by [G]turning, [D]turning we come [G]round right.
{end_of_chorus}
